{"kind":"assert","text":"Independent DESIGN findings, pending corrected artifact binding and normal guarded review filing; no review approval/adoption is asserted here.\n\nChecker full DESIGN assessment at5fa375edd27ebae89b0706adbce4cd7e0a260cab, treeb9411bd7d24a7c90b9244271c24f5db136bcb346. Root personally read all18054ASCII bytes/241LF in three gap-free bounded displays, SHA256d69e455e9808606eb828fac2a882fc02867411ae88f47b56fdf2487ed8561b33. Native metadata confirms the only change fromcf4e is this note. Exact subject47896; invitation1670/promise6b289. This is design assessment, not source approval, adoption or partial484/9be closure. Root owns independent verdict, lead order, producers implementation.\n\nThe design correctly treats data digests as insufficient executable identity, preserves both colliding legacy@1 histories, refuses unknown/mixed provenance without guessing, archives actual bytes rather than mutable exports, and keeps provider secrets outside bundles. It preserves pending duties and custody, selects an exact old/new root, and rejects rollback that drops admitted roots. These are useful foundations. They do not yet specify a safe executable boundary or complete revision activation.\n\nP1 — Define the historical/current authority boundary (V1,V3,V5,H3). Archive semantics for historical judgment and observation; independently preserve current strict43d read/session preparation, revocation, standing, deployment, named read and final post-await checks at the live transport/port boundary. The note currently requires archived authority/session/capability meaning and current standing without specifying precedence. Define an owner-reviewed operation table for pure historical verification, authorized raw history reads and live mutations/dispatch, identifying which bundle/current guards govern each. Older session code must not replace strict current checks; current helpers must not reinterpret old sealed acts or manufacture historical grants. Resolve bootstrap: V3 reads authenticated genesis/target before selecting the semantics needed by those guards. State the semantic-independent, authenticated path and its trust basis, with cheap checks before RPC and no grants/sealing/dispatch when unresolved. This is a contract clarification, not a demand for a new engine or tests now.\n\nP2 — Make binding identity and trust durable across deployment changes (V2-V4). Distinguish stable service identity, immutable birth/admission release and current deployed release. Define which one keys resolution so a rollout neither loses a valid old binding nor silently selects semantics by current deployment. Explain how witnessed-head coverage and evidence of continued implementation constrain later heads. Specify registry canonical/content identity, authenticated publisher/trust anchor, authorization and revision freshness/pinning/key rotation; explicit local-manifest use must visibly accept the same operator trust rather than trust scope-supplied data. FullScope/genesis/head ancestry alone is not a deployment-to-executable attestation. Keep the already named missing build/source, full-incarnation and retained-history evidence open; replay consistency cannot supply it.\n\nP2 — Activate one compatible revision set and retain original attempts (H3,H4). Specify a coherent activation tuple covering registry revision/digest, routing revision, bundle set and executing runtime. Define immutable binding identity and allowed amendments so dispatch, recovery, credential retrieval and cleanup for a retained attempt use its original provider/capability binding after restart or config change. State how already-running cached objects prove convergence or refuse affected work; observing one new Worker revision does not establish all cached object settings. Make the gate for new claims/roots concrete, prevent mixed revisions from sealing or sending, and keep compatible old duties served. Rollback must preserve the same invariant, not just a list with matching root names.\n\nMixed-history refusal is honest: it is preservation of records with paused semantics, not proof that every legacy room remains operational. Exact interval semantics need their later owner decision and cannot be smuggled in by replay matching. The candidate16-root limit is explicitly unadopted and unmeasured; choose root/manifest/reference-closure work bounds through the named capacity/contract owner before implementation. No numerical readiness finding follows from this design. The permanent semantic archive is a broad obligation; prefer a narrow immutable binding manifest and pure evaluator interface with explicit ports, rather than importing archived Worker bindings.\n\nRetained source assertions in the evidence table are qualified accurately. Actual full historical/build/head correspondence remains producer/operator evidence owed. This review used static note/native metadata and previously read durable records only; no project execution, generated histories, tests/gate, provider/private probes or source changes. Strengthen the existing proposed witnesses after adoption; do not create a duplicate task or matrix. Amend these decisions in the same design owner before implementation/adoption. Version/custody implementation and live validation remain separate open work.\n"}